<item>
            <title>[LU-20427] sanity-lnet.sh sets invalid subsystem_debug values</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20427</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20329&quot; title=&quot;debug fixes and improvements&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-20329&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-20329&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; patch &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/66451&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/66451&lt;/a&gt; dropped &quot;neterror net nettrace malloc&quot; arguments from set_default_debug and moved them to SUBSYSTEM environment variable at the top of sanity-lnet.sh, but SUBSYSTEM is the variable used to set subsystem_debug mask, not the debug mask. The correct variable is PTLDEBUG.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
